    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the two new fiscal-year checkpoints (Cp14, Cp48).\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts **1 July**), driving everything off the business-day-adjusted registration date already stored on the owner.\n\n**New shared utility** \u2014 `util/FiscalYear.java`:\n- `startYear(date)` \u2014 the fiscal year's starting calendar year (the date's year from 1 July onward, else the previous year).\n- `yearSegment(date)` \u2014 that start year mod 100 (the `<YY>`).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 the `'FY<YY>'` string.\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2014 elapsed fiscal years = number of 1-July boundaries crossed (difference of fiscal start years).\n\n**Wired in:**\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` mapping (`FiscalYear.label`) and switched the membership number's year segment from `getYear() % 100` to `FiscalYear.yearSegment(...)`, keeping the two in lockstep (what Cp14 asserts).\n- `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the audit line's membership number now uses the fiscal year segment too, so it stays consistent with the response.\n- `util/MembershipLevel.java` \u2014 tenure now counted in elapsed fiscal years (`FiscalYear.elapsed`, threshold `> 1` fiscal year) instead of a 365-day window; docs updated.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` schema property (regenerates `OwnerDto` with the getter/setter) and refreshed the `membershipNumber` / `membershipPoints` descriptions to describe the fiscal-year basis.\n\nBehaviour change is real: for a registration date before 1 July, the membership `<YY>` and `fiscalYear` now name the prior calendar year (e.g. 2026-03-15 \u2192 `FY25`), and tenure crossing a 1-July boundary \u2014 not a 365-day span \u2014 is what earns the tenure points. Newly created owners still have zero tenure, so the level-4 cap the existing tests rely on is preserved.",
